Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:34:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] mb/radxa/x4: Add a setup menu

With edk2 and SMMSTORE, select DRIVERS_OPTION_CFR_ENABLED and add:
- Devices: "Onboard eMMC". When it is off, mainboard init disables the
  eMMC device before FSP-S reads ScsEmmcEnabled, so the controller is
  turned off and neither the firmware nor the OS sees the eMMC.
- Devices: "Wi-Fi" and "Bluetooth". When off, ramstage drives the M.2
  card's W_DISABLE1# (GPP_E12) or W_DISABLE2# (GPP_A13) low. Wi-Fi off
  also takes root port 4 and its clock source 2 out of FSP-M and
  disables the port before FSP-S, so the card leaves PCI. The board has
  no pull-ups on these lines, so "on" keeps the stock pad config:
  GPP_E12 undriven, GPP_A13 driven high.
- Devices: "Network boot" (network_stack), off by default. When it is
  off, edk2 loads no network driver, so the firmware has no PXE or
  HTTP boot. The OS still sees the LAN.
- System: VT-d.
- Power: the PL1 and PL2 package power limits, 13 W and 25 W by
  default, and the power limit lock.
- Power: PCIe clock power management and PCH root port ASPM. ASPM
  is off by default, as in the devicetree.

edk2 stores the defaults on its first boot; until then the devicetree
values apply. The power limit defaults match the devicetree, so the
limits stay the same when that happens.

